<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan mulls easing banks' investment rules - paper.</title>
<headline>Taiwan mulls easing banks' investment rules - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Finance Ministry was considering relaxing rules on banks' investment in the property market, the Economic Daily News reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The paper said the ministry plans to revise the Banking Law to allow banks to invest in properties that they do not occupy and set a ceiling for such investment at 40 percent of each bank's net asset value.</p>
<p>Currently, the law only allows banks to purchase properties for their own use.</p>
<p>Officials declined to confirm the report, but said the ministry did not rule out such possibility.</p>
</text>
